Atlas overlay patch 0002: privacy/gpc-default-on
Why: Global Privacy Control is on for every profile, so pages see Sec-GPC: 1 and
navigator.globalPrivacyControl == true unless the person turns it off. The inherited series
already carries the pref and all of its consumers (request headers, renderer preferences, the
navigator and worker bindings) but registers it off; only the registered default changes
(patches-0 P-02).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
Test filter: *GlobalPrivacyControl*; journey J-A2 (Sec-GPC: 1, navigator.globalPrivacyControl)
Rebase risk: L (one line, in the hunk the inherited GPC pref patch adds)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunk in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
@@ -183,7 +183,7 @@
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
       prefs::kEnableDoNotTrack, true,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
-  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl, false);
+  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl, true);
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kPrintPreviewUseSystemDefaultPrinter,
                                 false);
